## Article 306. Preparation for appeal review

```catala
declaration scope Article306AppealPreparation:
  input check content AppealPreparationCheck
  output mayInvolveNonParticipant content YesNo
  output newEvidenceAdmissible content YesNo
  output writtenProceedingPossible content YesNo

scope Article306AppealPreparation:
# May involve non-participant whose rights affected
  label involve definition mayInvolveNonParticipant under condition
    check.nonParticipantRightsAffected = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_involve definition mayInvolveNonParticipant equals No

# New evidence admissible when justification valid
  label evidence_admissible definition newEvidenceAdmissible under condition
    check.newEvidenceRequested = Yes
    and check.newEvidenceJustificationValid = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label evidence_inadmissible definition newEvidenceAdmissible under condition
    check.newEvidenceRequested = Yes
    and check.newEvidenceJustificationValid = No
    consequence equals No

# Written proceeding possible when case can be decided on existing evidence
  label written definition writtenProceedingPossible under condition
    check.writtenProceedingAppropriate = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_written definition writtenProceedingPossible equals No
```

## Article 307. Scheduling appeal review

```catala
declaration scope Article307AppealScheduling:
  output caseScheduledAfterPreparation content YesNo

scope Article307AppealScheduling:
# Case scheduled for review after preparatory actions
  label scheduled definition caseScheduledAfterPreparation equals Yes
```

## Article 308. Scope of appeal review

```catala
declaration scope Article308AppealScope:
  input check content AppealReviewScope
  output reviewWithinComplaintGrounds content YesNo
  output mayGoBeyondComplaintGrounds content YesNo
  output newClaimsProhibited content YesNo

scope Article308AppealScope:
# Review within complaint grounds
  label within_grounds definition reviewWithinComplaintGrounds under condition
    check.withinComplaintGrounds = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# May go beyond complaint grounds for mandatory procedural violations or wrong law
  label beyond_grounds definition mayGoBeyondComplaintGrounds under condition
    check.mandatoryProceduralViolationFound = Yes
    or check.wrongSubstantiveLawFound = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_beyond definition mayGoBeyondComplaintGrounds equals No

# New claims not raised in first instance are prohibited
  label no_new_claims definition newClaimsProhibited under condition
    check.newClaimsNotRaisedInFirstInstance = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_new_issues definition newClaimsProhibited under condition
    check.newClaimsNotRaisedInFirstInstance = No
    consequence equals No
```

## Article 309. Timeline for appeal review

```catala
declaration scope Article309AppealTimeline:
  input check content AppealTimelineCheck
  output withinTimeLimit content YesNo
  output extensionAllowed content YesNo

scope Article309AppealTimeline:
# Resolution: 60 days from opening
  label resolution_timeline definition withinTimeLimit under condition
    check.appealingResolution = Yes
    and check.daysSinceOpening <= 60
    consequence equals Yes

  label resolution_exceeded definition withinTimeLimit under condition
    check.appealingResolution = Yes
    and check.daysSinceOpening > 60
    consequence equals No

# Ruling: 30 days from opening
  label ruling_timeline definition withinTimeLimit under condition
    check.appealingResolution = No
    and check.daysSinceOpening <= 30
    consequence equals Yes

  label ruling_exceeded definition withinTimeLimit under condition
    check.appealingResolution = No
    and check.daysSinceOpening > 30
    consequence equals No

# Extension up to 15 days in exceptional cases
  label extension definition extensionAllowed under condition
    check.extensionRequested = Yes
    and check.extensionDays <= 15
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_extension definition extensionAllowed equals No
```

## Article 310. Appeal review in court hearing

```catala
declaration scope Article310AppealHearing:
  output panelOfThreeRequired content YesNo
  output simplifiedProceedingRulesApply content YesNo
  output appellantSpeaksFirst content YesNo

scope Article310AppealHearing:
# Panel of three judges
  label three_judges definition panelOfThreeRequired equals Yes

# Simplified proceeding rules apply
  label simplified_rules definition simplifiedProceedingRulesApply equals Yes

# Appellant speaks first
  label appellant_first definition appellantSpeaksFirst equals Yes
```

## Article 311. Written appeal proceeding

```catala
declaration scope Article311AppealWritten:
  input check content AppealWrittenProceedingCheck
  output writtenProceedingAllowed content YesNo

scope Article311AppealWritten:
# Written proceeding when no hearing requested, no one appeared, or first instance was written simplified
  label no_request definition writtenProceedingAllowed under condition
    check.noParticipantRequestsHearing = Yes
    and check.caseCanBeDecidedOnExistingEvidence = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_appearance definition writtenProceedingAllowed under condition
    check.noParticipantAppeared = Yes
    and check.caseCanBeDecidedOnExistingEvidence = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label written_first_instance definition writtenProceedingAllowed under condition
    check.firstInstanceWasWrittenSimplified = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Grand Chamber may also proceed in writing
  label grand_chamber definition writtenProceedingAllowed under condition
    check.grandChamberAppeal = Yes
    and check.caseCanBeDecidedOnExistingEvidence = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_allowed definition writtenProceedingAllowed equals No
```

## Article 312. Appeal against first instance rulings

```catala
declaration scope Article312AppealAgainstRulings:
  output rulingAppealFollowsGeneralRules content YesNo
  output certainRulingsReviewedInWriting content YesNo

scope Article312AppealAgainstRulings:
# Ruling appeals follow general appeal rules with specific features
  label general_rules definition rulingAppealFollowsGeneralRules equals Yes

# Certain rulings reviewed in written proceeding
  label written_review definition certainRulingsReviewedInWriting equals Yes
```

## Article 313. Consequences of non-appearance

```catala
declaration scope Article313AppealNonAppearance:
  input check content AppealNonAppearanceCheck
  output reviewPostponed content YesNo
  output reviewProceedsWithoutParticipant content YesNo

scope Article313AppealNonAppearance:
# Postpone when participant not properly notified
  label not_notified definition reviewPostponed under condition
    check.participantProperlyNotified = No
    consequence equals Yes

# Postpone when good cause for absence
  label good_cause definition reviewPostponed under condition
    check.participantProperlyNotified = Yes
    and check.goodCauseForAbsence = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Proceed when properly notified and no good cause
  label proceed definition reviewProceedsWithoutParticipant under condition
    check.participantProperlyNotified = Yes
    and check.goodCauseForAbsence = No
    and check.participationMandatory = No
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_postponed definition reviewPostponed equals No

  label must_attend definition reviewProceedsWithoutParticipant under condition
    check.participationMandatory = Yes
    and check.goodCauseForAbsence = No
    consequence equals No
```

## Article 314. Claim withdrawal and reconciliation during appeal

```catala
declaration scope Article314AppealReconciliation:
  input check content AppealReconciliationCheck
  output withdrawalOrReconciliationAllowed content YesNo
  output firstInstanceDecisionInvalidated content YesNo

scope Article314AppealReconciliation:
# Plaintiff may withdraw, parties may reconcile at any time before appeal ends
  label allowed definition withdrawalOrReconciliationAllowed under condition
    check.withdrawalOrReconciliationValid = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_allowed definition withdrawalOrReconciliationAllowed under condition
    check.withdrawalOrReconciliationValid = No
    consequence equals No

# First instance decision invalidated upon withdrawal or reconciliation
  label invalidated definition firstInstanceDecisionInvalidated under condition
    check.withdrawalOrReconciliationValid = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_invalidated definition firstInstanceDecisionInvalidated equals No
```
